          "end": 3.98,
          "relative_start": 0.08,
          "relative_end": 3.98,
          "en": "What's coming next for Cuba? Catcher, Caleb, still in haunches?",
          "zh": "古巴接下来会怎样？捕手凯勒还在蹲着吗？",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "古巴接下来会怎样"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "What's coming next for Cuba"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "start": 3.98,
          "end": 11.58,
          "relative_start": 3.98,
          "relative_end": 11.58,
          "en": "I just can't tell you that. We've got options all over the map. Perhaps no other nation epitomizes Cold War politics more than Cuba.",
          "zh": "我无法告诉你。我们有各种选择。也许没有哪个国家比古巴更能代表冷战政治。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "冷战政治"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "Cold War politics"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "start": 11.58,
          "end": 17.58,
          "relative_start": 11.58,
          "relative_end": 17.58,
          "en": "When you look for a country that's, let's say, punched above its weight on a global stage, Cuba should be on the list.",
          "zh": "说到在全球舞台上发挥超常影响力的国家，古巴应有一席之地。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "全球舞台上发挥超常影响力"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "punched above its weight on a global stage"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 25.58,
          "relative_start": 17.58,
          "relative_end": 25.58,
          "en": "Cuba and the United States by default of their geography have always had some kind of economic relationship.",
          "zh": "古巴和美国由于地理邻近，一直存在某种经济关系。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "经济关系"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "economic relationship"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "start": 25.58,
          "end": 28.88,
          "relative_start": 25.58,
          "relative_end": 28.88,
          "en": "When we had prohibition in the United States, Cuba became a haven.",
          "zh": "美国禁酒令时期，古巴成了避风港。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "避风港"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "haven"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 6,
          "start": 28.88,
          "end": 33.28,
          "relative_start": 28.88,
          "relative_end": 33.28,
          "en": "For American tourists. Cuba is just not even miles south of Florida.",
          "zh": "对美国游客来说，古巴距佛罗里达南部仅几英里。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "距佛罗里达南部仅几英里"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "miles south of Florida"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 7,
          "start": 33.28,
          "end": 38.58,
          "relative_start": 33.28,
          "relative_end": 38.58,
          "en": "It's in the heart of the Caribbean. It's been seen as kind of a strategic platform for U.S. rivals.",
          "zh": "它位于加勒比海心脏，被视为美国对手的战略平台。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "战略平台"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "strategic platform"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 8,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 45.38,
          "relative_start": 38.58,
          "relative_end": 45.38,
          "en": "The U.S. has had a broad trade embargo on Cuba since shortly after the revolution in the 1960s.",
          "zh": "自1960年代革命后不久，美国就对古巴实施了广泛贸易禁运。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "贸易禁运"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "trade embargo"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 9,
          "start": 45.38,
          "end": 53.38,
          "relative_start": 45.38,
          "relative_end": 53.38,
          "en": "Cuba is ruled by a single party, the Cuban Communist Party, and it controls the legislature, controls the military, controls all facets of society.",
          "zh": "古巴由古巴共产党一党统治，控制立法、军队和社会方方面面。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "一党统治"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "ruled by a single party"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 10,
          "start": 54.38,
          "end": 62.38,
          "relative_start": 54.38,
          "relative_end": 62.38,
          "en": "But the socialist idealism that burst Cuba has grown to a halt, literally running out of gas.",
          "zh": "但曾蓬勃发展的社会主义理想已停滞，literally 燃油耗尽。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "社会主义理想已停滞"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "socialist idealism"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 11,
          "start": 62.38,
          "end": 68.38,
          "relative_start": 62.38,
          "relative_end": 68.38,
          "en": "There is a dire jet fuel shortage in Cuba. The U.S. is moving to cut off the country's oil supply.",
          "zh": "古巴面临严重的航空燃油短缺。美国正试图切断该国的石油供应。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "航空燃油短缺"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "jet fuel shortage",
            "cut off the country's oil supply"
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 12,
          "start": 68.38,
          "end": 72.88,
          "relative_start": 68.38,
          "relative_end": 72.88,
          "en": "The crippling blackouts and a teetering economy have sparked unrest on the island.",
          "zh": "严重的停电和摇摇欲坠的经济引发了岛上的动荡。",
          "zh_highlights": [
            "停电",
            "动荡"
          ],
          "en_highlights": [
            "crippling blackouts",
            "unrest"
          ]
        },
        {
